84.5,6.7 179.4,6.8 174.4,6.7 169.4,6.7 164.3,6.8 159.2,6.9 154,7.1 149.1,6.7 143.9,6.9 138.9,6.7 133.9,6.7 128.8,6.8 123.8,6.6 118.6,6.6 113.7,6.3 108.5,6.5 103.4,6.3 98.4,6.3 93.3,6.4 88.3,6.3 83.2,6.2 78.2,6.1 73,6.4 68.1,6.1 63,6.3 57.8,6.3 52.8,6.2 47.7,6.5 42.8,6.4 37.7,6.6 32.7,6.5 27.5,6.8 22.4,6.9 17.4,6.9 12.3,7.2 7.4,7.1 2.6,7.3 .1,7.5 -.2,7.4 -.5,7.2 -.8,7 -1,6.8 -1.2,6.5 -1.3,6.1 -1.3,5.7 -1.2,5.4 -1,5.1 -.7,4.8 -.4,4.6 -.1,4.5 .1,4.5Z"/></svg><p class="look-lede">What this server limits. A request over a limit is refused with the number it reached and the limit, and nothing of it is kept.</p><div class="look-table" role="region" aria-label="Limits" tabindex="0"><table><caption>Limits</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Limit</th><th scope="col">Value</th><th scope="col">At the limit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Stored per account</th><td>1 GiB</td><td>A deploy that would take the account over this is refused whole: nothing of it is published.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Builds a day per account</th><td>60</td><td>A build requested over this waits for the next day: the request is refused, and no build is queued.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sites per account</th><td>10</td><td>A new site over this is refused; the sites the account has are unchanged.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Deploys kept per site</th><td>20</td><td>Older deploys are removed, with the files only they used, when a newer one is published.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Time for one build</th><td>10 minutes</td><td>A build is given this long; the queue gives it to no one else before.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></main></div></body></html>
